     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">Hi Shengli,</span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\"> </span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">I am a little confused about the following words on how to\r\ncalculate the p-value of DMR:</span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\"> </span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">Based on the refined regions, we calculated</span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">the significance of the regions by combining the</span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">p-values of DMCs within that region. We used the</span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">dependence adjustment of the Stouffer-Liptak test to</span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">combine p-values [22,23].</span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><i><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\"> </span></i></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">For some CpG, the low-p is because case has lower methylation\r\nrate than control, however, for some other CpGs, the case has higher\r\nmethylation rate. If we only combine the p-value, how can we know in this\r\nregion, it is significant? For example, for a 10 cpgs region, 5 have higher\r\nmethylation rate, 5 have lower methylation rate for case, the result should be\r\ncanceled if we consider the region. But if you combine the CpG p value, it will\r\nbe significant. Did you consider the direction of significant in your software?  Thanks!</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\"><br></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;font-size:11pt\">Gengsheng</span></div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></div>"
    ]
